              "value": "Generate a valid oraInfoDisplay multiCardWidget using the enriched cost processing errors from {{$context.$nodes.BUNDLE_ERROR_ANALYSIS_RESULTS.$output.result.errorsByCode}}.\n\nEach property in `errorsByCode` is keyed by ErrorCode. For each entry, create one card using the entry payload:\n- `badgeText`: \"Error\"\n- `variant`: \"error\"\n- `subject`: use `Message`; if missing, use the ErrorCode.\n- `subtitle`: \"Transaction Count: \" followed by `ErrorCount` and \"Estimated Financial Impact\" followed by `-`, separated by `|` in readable text.\n- `summary`: copy the provided `summary` field exactly as the card summary, preserving all blank lines and `---` divider lines. The summary already contains Hotspots, Likely Root Cause, and Recommended Actions for that specific error code.\n\nDo not generate new root-cause analysis in this rendering node. Do not remove or rewrite divider lines from the summary. Do not use hardcoded sample cards. Generate cards only from the enriched errors object. If there are no entries, return a valid multiCardWidget with an empty cards array.\n\nReturn only the oraInfoDisplay markup with valid JSON inside it, using this shape. Always include `layoutMode`: \"single-col\" so cards render in one column:\n```\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"error-cards\">\n{\n  \"patternId\": \"multiCardWidget\",\n   \"title\": \"Cost Processing Errors for Process {{$context.$variables.latestCostProcessRequestId}}\",\n   \"subtitle\": \"{{$context.$nodes.BUNDLE_ERROR_ANALYSIS_RESULTS.$output.result.count}} error types found. Review each card for transaction counts, likely causes, and recommended actions.\",\n  \"config\": {\n    \"layoutMode\": \"single-col\",\n    \"cards\": []\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n```"
            }
          ],
